// Cloudflare Workers config for the SignalDesk frontend: static assets, plus a
// small script (worker/index.js) whose only extra job is a Cron Trigger that
// pings the Render API so it is awake when visitors arrive.
//
// Live at https://signaldesk.shyamsundar2935.workers.dev, built by Cloudflare
// Workers Builds with Root directory = /frontend:
//   build:            npm run build           -> ./dist
//   production (main): npx wrangler deploy
//   other branches:   npx wrangler versions upload   (uploads a version, not live)
//
// Before this file existed, `wrangler deploy` on main inferred the setup, but
// `wrangler versions upload` cannot, so every pull-request build failed with
// "Missing entry-point to Worker script or to assets directory". This file
// states the same setup explicitly for both commands.
//
// not_found_handling = single-page-application matches the live behaviour
// (verified 2026-11-10: unknown paths such as /stocks/RELIANCE.NS return
// index.html with 200) so React Router deep links keep working.
//
// VITE_API_BASE is NOT set here: it is a build-time variable held in the
// Worker's Build settings and baked into the bundle by `vite build`.
//
// Cron: every 10 minutes from 02:00 to 18:59 UTC (07:30-00:30 IST). Not 24/7:
// Render's free tier allows 750 instance-hours a month across all free
// services and always-on would use ~744. This window uses ~520.
{
  "name": "signaldesk",
  "main": "worker/index.js",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-11-01",
  "assets": {
    "directory": "./dist",
    "binding": "ASSETS",
    "not_found_handling": "single-page-application"
  },
  "triggers": {
    "crons": ["*/10 2-18 * * *"]
  },
  "observability": { "enabled": true }
}
